## Spec: Skip Link — Visible on Focus

**Priority:** Medium UX
**Affects:** exam.html line 149, shared/styles.css .sr-only class

### Problem
exam.html has a skip link: `<a href="#questionsContainer" class="sr-only">Skip to questions</a>`

Using `.sr-only` makes the link invisible at all times — including when focused by keyboard. This means sighted keyboard users (Tab through the page) see focus jump to an invisible element, causing confusion.

The correct pattern: skip links should be visually hidden by DEFAULT but visible when focused.

### Fix

Add a utility class to shared/styles.css:

```css
.skip-link {
  position: absolute;
  top: -40px;
  left: 0;
  padding: 8px 16px;
  background: var(--color-primary, #1D42BA);
  color: #FFFFFF;
  font-size: var(--text-sm, 14px);
  font-weight: 600;
  text-decoration: none;
  z-index: 9999;
  transition: top 0.15s ease;
}
.skip-link:focus-visible {
  top: 0;
}
```

In exam.html, change the skip link class from `sr-only` to `skip-link`.

### State Machine
States: hidden | visible
Variables: isFocused (boolean)
Transitions:
- hidden -> visible: user tabs to skip link (focus-visible)
- visible -> hidden: user tabs away (blur) OR clicks the link (navigates away)

### Visual Spec
- Background: `--color-primary` (#1D42BA)
- Text: white (#FFFFFF)
- Size: 8px 16px padding, --text-sm font
- Position: slides in from top-left at top:0 on focus
- Transition: 0.15s ease (within approved 150ms micro range)
- prefers-reduced-motion: set transition to 0ms

### Acceptance Criteria
1. Pressing Tab on exam.html causes the skip link to appear at top-left of viewport
2. Skip link text reads 'Skip to questions'
3. Pressing Enter on the skip link moves focus to #questionsContainer
4. Tabbing away hides the skip link again
5. Skip link is fully hidden when not focused (no layout shift)
6. In prefers-reduced-motion: no slide animation (instant show/hide)

### What NOT to Change
- .sr-only class (other elements use it for screen-reader-only labels)
- All other exam.html content
- The skip link destination (#questionsContainer)
